metadata.method:
a continuous index field t(u, v) in native texel units, sampled at every output pixel centre:
  * background: native index (black; E/F kept);
  * band rows: left edge = one straight anti-aliased line per band, fitted INSIDE the native boundary constraints
    (texel L-1 centre outside, texel L centre inside, for every row) - verified feasible per band;
  * fascia rows (low roughness): isotonic (monotone non-decreasing) fit of the native row, gaussian-smoothed, linear in u;
  * window rows (high roughness): each native texel becomes a pane (inset frame 1/8 texel each side, frame index =
    max(native, smooth fascia level) + 2, capped 13), horizontally adjacent texels whose index differs by <= 1 merge
    into one wider pane; pane interior keeps the native texel index with a 0.5-index lighter top (ceiling light);
  * every native texel centre pixel floor((i+0.5)*scale) is stamped with the native index (exact colour and class).
RGB = lerp(P[floor t], P[ceil t]); alpha = categorical class of the nearest index (0 raw 0x0000 / 127 / 255 STP).
